<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9514"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sidewalker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sidewalker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 2:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I will say, that I never posted or talked about what I thought this guy would look like. <BR>But in my minds eye......I somehow thought he would look just as he did. A bit overweight &#40;not certain of this, but he seems broad in the chest&#41; and bald, or getting a really large forehead so to speak&#41; I did expect him to wear glasses tho. <BR> <BR> <BR>I did think he was still employed. It does not surprise me, in the least his profession. Out there but not really seen. Not a policeman, but worked semi close with them. It figures he is a neat freak. It just figures.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9514-->
<!--Post: 9539--><!--Time: 1109548842-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9539"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 4:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A preliminary assessment of my psychological portrait of the BTK Strangler suggests a few hits and misses. The comparison between appearance and reality can be found below: <BR> <BR>Age <BR> <BR>I did not believe the BTK Strangler was 65 years of age. He would never disclose his age. Disposing of the cereal box in a rural locale confirmed in my mind he was younger than a pensioner. Between 50 and 56 years of age was a possibility. It was close but did not yield a cigar. <BR> <BR>Race <BR> <BR>The BTK Strangler&#39;s strong desire to convince the Wichita Police Department, the media and public he was hispanic suggested he was most probably caucasian. I relied heavily on the witness account of the woman who supposedly saw the BTK Strangler deliver a correspondence in the early hours in June 1979. <BR> <BR>Residence <BR> <BR>The locale of the crimes in the city of Wichita suggested the BTK Strangler was a local. His knowledge of local enterprises and his confidence to report the murder of Nancy Fox supported the hypothesis. <BR> <BR>Education <BR> <BR>I strongly believed the BTK Strangler graduated from Wichita State University. This belief was based on his references to instructors at the university and placing a correspondence in the library. If, the suspect mentioned he graduated with a PhD from Wichita State University in his correspondences, I would have doubted the authenticity of the claim. Majoring in the physical sciences or engineering was incorrect. This claim was based on the mathematical ability demonstrated by the suspect in correspondences. <BR> <BR>Church <BR> <BR>I believed he attended church from early childhood. Attending church would create a facade of respectability among the community. His communications in the past year with the themes of omnipotence and omnipresence suggested a belief he was godlike. <BR> <BR>Family <BR> <BR>I do not have sufficient information at the moment on his family to compare it with my portrait. <BR> <BR>Intelligence <BR> <BR>Its too early to assess his intelligence. He may have an Intelligence Quotient of 130. It seems his Intelligence Quotient could be closer to 120. <BR> <BR>Military <BR> <BR>He did serve in the miliary. I do not know, if the suspect served in combat at this moment. <BR> <BR>Photography <BR> <BR>The suspect is an avid photographer. It allowed him to indulge in voyeurism. It also allowed him to film his neighbors. <BR> <BR>Marriage <BR> <BR>I believed the suspect was married. Married life allowed him to project a facade of respectability. During the 1970s when the FBI Behavioral Science Unit began utilizing forensic psychology, most of the profiles suggested sadistic serial murderers were single men. It could have allowed the suspect to avoid being considered a person of interest. Two adult children was correct. <BR> <BR>Victims <BR> <BR>The oedipal complex seems to be the motive for murdering women who were mothers. It seems he wanted to resolve his hatred for his mother by murdering them. I believed he did not stop murdering after admitting to the murder of Vicki Wegerle. I suspect more unsolved murders will be connected to the suspect. <BR> <BR>No previous Criminal Record <BR> <BR>The suspect&#39;s confidence in resuming communication with the Wichita Police Department and the media suggested he did not have a criminal record. <BR> <BR>Employment <BR> <BR>I did not include this in my psychological portrait of the BTK Strangler. I have mentioned in previous messages the suspect could have been employed by Wichita State Univeristy as a tutor. It proved incorrect. I found it difficult to reach a decision on his current position in the portrait. <BR> <BR>I did not believe the BTK Strangler would be captured. It proved to be an incorrect assertion. <BR> <BR>I suppose studying economics and econometrics at the big H and HBS does not prepare an individual for the world of forensic science and forensic psychology. At 28, I have a few more years to refine my technique and look forward to Beattie&#39;s book.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
