<!--Post: 9540--><!--Time: 1109549871-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9540"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 4:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m still waiting to hear more biographic info on DR, there&#39;s still a lot of unanswered questions.  For example the Hispanic issue -- the original DNA that LE was working with must&#39;ve indicated some Hispanic lineage, otherwise WPD wouldn&#39;t have gone after Mr. V. in December.  So what&#39;s the Hispanic connection in DR&#39;s background? <BR> <BR>I&#39;m also waiting for more details to come out about DR&#39;s employment history, and especially his military history.   <BR> <BR>But for what it&#39;s worth, here are the new facts that have surprised me:   <BR> <BR>- Overtly bullying so many people around him -- I  assumed he&#39;d have been more smooth in his relations with other people, instead of cultivating so many enemies, but maybe he just got crotchety as he got older and it was the only way he could get cheap thrills, by aggravating every other person in the neighbourhood <BR> <BR>- Chose victims that lived in close proximity to him, like, really close proximity: the victim who lived practically right across the street from him. Reminds me of how many child killers know their victims and take them right out of their homes. <BR> <BR>- Dog catcher:  I still can&#39;t get over this one.  I was picturing an engineer, a computer programmer, or something else more technical, due to his obsession with coded messages, etc.  At least the dogs of Wichita can sleep in peace now. <BR> <BR>- Married for 30 years, with two grown kids:  I never would&#39;ve guessed that he could have had kids.  I thought he would&#39;ve been too sexually dysfunctional.  Makes me think his murders were motivated more by sadism at the core, and perhaps certain specific things that he included in his b-t-k routine were what gave him a sexual thrill on top of it. <BR> <BR>- Church council president -- but I guess if you&#39;re going to be a wolf in sheep&#39;s clothing, why not go the whole nine yards. <BR> <BR>- Some profilers had guessed that during the early to mid 1970s he may have been into the music/poetry scene around WSU, which I thought sounded pretty plausible because of his poetry, but he was a square all the way.  BTW, have you seen his Air Force photo?  Creepy. <BR> <BR>- He actually has military experience.  I thought he was fantasizing about that one and was just a wannabe. <BR> <BR>I want to see what was included in all of his communications with LE.  Should be plenty of enlightening tidbits in there.  Or maybe just more murky detritus from a warped mind. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9540-->
<!--Post: 9588--><!--Time: 1109560830-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9588"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lubbock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lubbock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 7:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Who: <BR>Anger clouds judgement. One would think that you would at least try to be fair. <BR> <BR>- Gravelly quality creeping into his voice with age? I haven&#39;t heard him speak recently. This would also be subjective in the ear of the beholder. <BR> <BR>- No he didn&#39;t serve in Nam, he did a tour in Korea while in the Air Force. Working on aircraft? In the rear with the gear? <BR> <BR>- Small to medium build? Strong? Unremarkable facial features? These are also subjective. People tend to thicken as they age &#40;in your case it happened between the ears&#41;. <BR> <BR>- Went to college on the G.I. bill? Changed majors? May not have graduated &#40;you&#39;ll notice that I qualified that opinion with &#34;may&#34;&#41;. You ought to share his college transcripts, surely you have them. <BR> <BR>- I stand by my assertion that he knew people on a superficial level. Maybe you and he were tight, I don&#39;t know. It does seem that none of his close friends were aware of a rather significant facet of his psyche. <BR> <BR>- Learning disabled? You have his early school records too I assume. By the way, people can overcome learning disabilities. <BR> <BR>- He has changed jobs a few times before ending up a glorified dog catcher with a degree in justice administration. <BR> <BR>- No-nonsense and humorless, but can affect a disarming charm &#40;or words to that effect&#41;. That seems fairly accurate, depending on who you listen to. <BR> <BR>- I still believe he has felt that his true genius has gone under-recognized. <BR> <BR>- He becomes defensive when questioned? I guess that too would depend on who you talked to. <BR> <BR>- He frequents parks &#40;the crux of my assertion&#41; would seem to be true, even if it was within the context of his job. He may have fished the local ponds, walked, etc. - but you and his other close friends would be in a better position to know. <BR> <BR>- He doesn&#39;t drink? Again, I defer to your infinite and intimate knowlege of him. <BR> <BR>- Prostate cancer? You have his medical records too? <BR> <BR>Granted, I missed some totally. <BR> <BR>I am not rude, I merely reflect back. <BR> <BR>I admit to being a poor typist, and have some spelling issues too, but if it were important I&#39;d take the time to check and proof-read. As for my creativity, acumen at developing a plot and characters with depth, and ability to spin a compelling narrative, I guess that&#39;s for the readers to decide. <BR> <BR>By the way, the threats you e-mailed me are bordering on harassment. <BR> <BR>Peace, out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9588-->
<!--Post: 9807--><!--Time: 1109647746-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9807"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 7:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m going to keep my day job - not sure I&#39;m ready for the move to profiler. But then, to be fair to all of us, we sure didn&#39;t have the same information to work with that WPD had.   <BR> <BR>There are several of you that I truly believe could have caught this guy if you&#39;d have had access to the same info that WPD had, so kudos to you all. <BR> <BR>One more thing that might be dead wrong but... <BR> <BR>I think this group, as well as others, perhaps, spun BTK out of control and ultimately led to his capture.  So if anyone can take credit, I think all the amateur sleuths who obviously annoyed the hell out of WPD can take their bows for a job well done.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9807-->
<!--Post: 12201--><!--Time: 1111758518-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12201"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 5:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have recently begun to realize that I am a scarier mo-fo than I thought.  <BR> <BR>At ks.com, the &#34;Eagle Board&#34; I posted as a_bracksis, Lrry_Andrsn &#40;Larry Anderson&#41;, and thundersaid.  <BR> <BR>I went back and re-examined some old entries. I scared the pee out me. <BR> <BR> <BR><i>From: a_bracksis <b>Dec-4 &#40;2004&#41;</b> 3:01 am <BR>To: enixer &#40;13 of 70&#41; <BR>4291.13 in reply to 4291.1 <BR> <BR>&#34;Enixer; <BR> <BR>Ich denke, daï¿½ Sie absolut Recht haben. &#40;transl. I think you are absolutely right ~ LA.&#41; <BR> <BR><b>I think perfection, cleanliness, order, are all extremely important to him.</b> I think he may be into geneaology, at least a little, because his german ancestry is a very proud point with him. <BR> <BR><b>I think in his own mind he has a definite moral code, and may still go to church regularly. If not, I bet he knows his bible cold. He is either an evangelical lutheran or perhaps even a southern baptist, though that will not be the denomination he was familiar with growing up.</b> <BR> <BR><b>I wonder if he worked a job for a good deal of his life that he regarded as far beneath him, his intellect. I would think it was a job that required cleanliness and order, and though he knew the job was beneath him he still took great pride in these two things.</b> <BR> <BR><b>I bet he more closely resembles the mustached, &#39;dark&#39; drawing, but has probably always resented the inference he might be latino or perhaps Italian.</b> Germans are, as an archetype, blonde, and he may have even experimented with dyeing his hair, but possibly not liked the results...&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>Link to the original post, and I remind y&#39;all - edits to posts at ks.com are stamped with the date of edit, and you can&#39;t delete those, as far as I know. Just backin&#39; myself up here. - Link; <a href="http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag=kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=4291.13">Message # 4291.13</a>. <BR> <BR>It gets stranger. <BR> <BR><i>From: a_bracksis <b>Dec-12 &#40;2004&#41;</b> 11:21 pm <BR>To: talons &#40;13 of 23&#41; <BR>4572.13 in reply to 4572.1 <BR> <BR>&#34;....when I read tech school I instinctively <b>thought of the Air Force tech school in Wichita Falls, TX.<u>It&#39;s one of those danged gut things on my part</u></b>, and the bias I referred to might be the fact my own Dad studied there in the early 70&#39;s. <b>There is just some ineffable nagging thing there that keeps telling me air force.</b> I feel it may be something I&#39;ve unconsciously observed and just can&#39;t pin down yet...&#34;</i> Link; <a href="http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag=kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=4572.13">Message #4572.13</a>. To be fair...the &#34;Talons&#34; I was responding to prompted the response with a pretty impressive post of his/her own, one that deserves further linkage - <a href="http://forums.prospero.com/kr-kansas_news/messages?msg=4572.1">Message #4572.1</a> <BR> <BR>But here&#39;s the strangest. I posted the following as thundersaid in a thread that was humorously asking for &#34;psychic impressions&#34; of BTK. Earlier in that thread I posted a variation on my &#34;profile&#34;, with some added in stuff that was pretty off just like everyone else...then I posted the following: <BR> <BR><i>From: thundersaid <b>Feb-3 &#40;2005&#41;</b> 12:25 pm <BR>To: Vigilant &#40;11 of 26&#41; <BR>5627.11 in reply to 5627.9 <BR> <BR>&#34;...dreams, just ideas, gutfeelings, or just plain results from a &#34;hyper focus&#34; google-week or so? <BR> <BR>All of the above, actually. Well, perhaps not the &#39;dreams&#39; - I have fortunately had no dreams about BTK. <b>I had a malevolent daydream once where an older, balding gentleman with dark hair and a mustache, who was a bit jowly and wearing a tan members-only style jacket over a yellow and red plaid shirt, wore aviator-frame prescription glasses with a tint &#40;not sunglasses, but regular glasses that perhaps darkened in the sunlight&#41;, was standing on the driveway outside, staring at me through the bedroom window. This approximated a vision, I suppose, as I did not actually perceive him there - that would have been psychosis - but had the image of this man come so vividly and forcefully into my mind that the hair stood up on the back of my neck and I forced myself to get away from the computer and watch a South Park DVD...&#34;</b></i> Link; <a href="http://forums.prospero.com/kr-kansas_news/messages?msg=5627.11">Message #5627.11</a>. <BR> <BR>Am I tooting my own horn? I guess it looks that way... but it&#39;s not intended that way, actually. For one thing, nothing that I hit on, given to a law enforcement officer beforehand, would necessarily have helped find BTK/Rader.  <BR> <BR>But for another thing - I&#39;m simply trying to figure out how I could get so close in some respects and see if I can reproduce that in the future. Re-trace my mental steps, so to speak. Suggestions there are welcome, if any.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
