<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12246"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 6:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Elsewhere is right. <BR> <BR>Don&#39;t think too hard. Concentration is highly over-rated. Think a thought clearly, then let it go&#40;sleeping works particularly well&#41;. The subconcsious is where the mojo happens.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12246-->
